course: dictionary
lesson: 8801
title: Shatter and its meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Shatter is a verb, and it has several meanings. Its main meaning is to break suddenly into many small pieces. «The window shattered when the lightning hit the tree.» The window did not slowly crack. It broke all at once into pieces.
explain: Context tells you which meaning fits. «The silence was shattered by a loud bang.» You cannot break silence into pieces, so here shatter means the quiet was suddenly destroyed. Test it: "the quiet was suddenly ended" makes sense.
explain: Shatter can also mean to beat a record by a lot, or to make someone very upset or very tired. Look at the words around it to choose the right meaning, and try your meaning in the sentence to check.
fact: Shatter is a verb: shatter, shatters, shattered, shattering.
fact: «Shatter» means to break suddenly into many small pieces.
fact: «Shatter» can also mean to destroy something suddenly, such as hope or calm.
fact: «Shatter a record» means to beat it by a lot.
fact: Glass shatters, so stay away from broken glass and tell an adult.
exercise: «The window shattered when lightning struck the tree.» What does shattered mean here? | Felt very calm | Opened slowly | *Broke suddenly into many small pieces | Turned a bright colour
exercise: «The silence was shattered by a loud bang.» What does shattered mean here? | *Suddenly destroyed, so the quiet ended | Made softer and gentler | Painted a new colour
exercise: Why should you stay away from broken glass? | It is warm and soft | It is a good place to play | *It can cut you, so tell an adult
test: «The runner shattered the old record by three seconds.» What does shattered mean? | Broke it into pieces | Forgot it | Dropped it on the track | *Beat it by a lot
test: Which of these is least likely to shatter? | A window | *A metal spoon, which can be bent without breaking | A china cup | A glass jar
exam: In the cartoon, Tom «shatters into pieces and pops back into shape», but what is true in real life? | Real people shatter and pop back into shape like cartoons | Real bones never break | Real people are flattened like pancakes and feel nothing | *Real bones can break, and a broken bone needs a doctor
